ng labs\nStaff\nNews\nContact us\nLiverpool Women in Science & Engineering\nOutreach\nResources for teachers\nGirls into Electronics\nVice Chancellor\u2019s Engineering Fellowships. Now Open.\nThe university is offering five-year Engineering Fellowships to support ambitious researchers in developing world-leading research and driving innovation.\nFind out more\nhome\nSchool of Engineering\nWelcome to the School of Engineering\nSteeped in history. Bursting with ambition to shape a better future.\nWe have been advancing engineering since 1886. Hele-Shaw flow, crucial in fluid mechanics, was even named after our School founder - Professor Henry Hele-Shaw. Today, Liverpool Engineers across our four departments continue to power global change. Rated 6th in the UK for our outstanding research impact, we are advancing Industry 4.0 through Additive Manufacturing, tackling pressing challenges in space research, leading biomedical breakthroughs and much more.\nOur hands-on and collaborative approach to teaching fosters these high standards in our students, equipping them to lead the impactful innovations of the future.\n6th\nin the UK for outstanding research impact\n94.4%\nof recent graduates in highly skilled roles\nTop 15\nranking for all our undergraduate engineering degrees\nWatch on YouTube: What is it like being a Liverpool Engineer?\nWhat is it like being a Liverpool Engineer?\nWe believe in the power of engineering to shape a better world. Take a look inside the School of Engineering and discover what it means to be a Liverpool Engineer.\nStudy with us\nWe are problem solvers seeking solutions to a huge range of challenges. Study with us, and make a difference.\nResearch\nRated 6th in the UK for our outstanding research impact, we are moving the needle on key global issues.\nFacilities\nWe believe you learn best by doing, which is why we have invested so heavily in top-tier facilities to help you experiment and learn.\nNews\nRead more news\nSection footer\nSchool of 